CORE gcc-only
conditional.c

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Null pointer constants in the conditional operator: an expression that
simplifies to 0 is a null pointer constant only if it is an integer constant
expression (C11 6.3.2.3p3, 6.6p6). GCC and Clang agree with every assertion.
Linux's __is_constexpr and is_const rely on this (#7927).
